※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=5300
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 5300 LANG_HOST_IN_AN_EXECUTABLE

※ A function the host defines is found by asking the program this one was
※ loaded into.  An executable is loaded into nothing -- the kernel starts it --
※ so there is nobody to ask, and the function is refused where it is declared
※ rather than left to fail at the first call.

@[host("puts")]
fn puts(text: str) → i32

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    if puts("hello") ≥ 0i32: 0u6 else: 1u6
